{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS2HYLfNXvwsgYHtMF5b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018gcgYxBHJ8FvsGK57byssw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-L1Pw6L && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('''DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\n''','')\ns=s.replace('''    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    if not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n''','''    # Intervals.icu returns neither expires_in nor refresh_token: the token does not expire\n    # (it lives until the athlete revokes it). Only schedule expiry if the provider says so.\n    expires_in = int(tok[\"expires_in\"]) if tok.get(\"expires_in\") else None\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n''')\ns=s.replace('\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in,','\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in if expires_in else None,')\ns=s.replace('''c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:''','''c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] is None or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:''')\ns=s.replace('''expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]))''','''expires_at=now + int(tok[\"expires_in\"]) if tok.get(\"expires_in\") else None)''')\ns=s.replace('''        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()''','''        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/url\":\n            return self.auth_init(as_json=True)''')\ns=s.replace('''    def auth_init(self):''','''    # The SPA calls /auth/url via fetch (so the Bearer header is sent) and then navigates\n    # to the returned URL; a plain link navigation cannot carry the Authorization header.\n    def auth_init(self, as_json=False):''')\ns=s.replace('''        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))''','''        url = AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\")\n        if as_json:\n            return self.send_json(200, {\"url\": url})\n        self.redirect(url)''')\nopen('server.py','w').write(s)\nc=open('config.py').read()\nc=c.replace('SCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"','# Scopes known to be accepted by Intervals (the 2026-09 grant). The CALENDAR:* scopes added\\n# on 2026-10-02 make the authorize step return 400 invalid_request.\\nSCOPES = \"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ\"')\nopen('config.py','w').write(c)\na=open('static/app.js').read()\na=a.replace('<a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a>','<button class=\"btn\" id=\"connect\">Connect Intervals.icu</button>')\na=a.replace('''    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''','''    const cb = document.getElementById(\"connect\");\n    if (cb) cb.onclick = async () => {\n      try { location.href = (await api(\"/api/intervals/auth/url\")).url; }\n      catch (e) { root.innerHTML = `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`; }\n    };\n    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''')\nopen('static/app.js','w').write(a)\nE\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Why Intervals.icu connection fails\n\n1. **Connect button always 401s.** It was a plain `<a href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">`. A browser navigation cannot send the `Authorization: Bearer` header (the token lives in localStorage and is only attached by the SPA's `fetch` wrapper), so the server answered `{\"error\":\"unauthorized\"}`. Fix: the button now calls `/api/intervals/auth/url` via `fetch` (header included), gets the authorize URL as JSON and navigates there. `/auth/init` still works for API clients.\n2. **Authorize step returns 400 `invalid_request`.** Since the 2026-10-02 calendar sync, `config.SCOPES` also requests `CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE`; the only successful grant (Rivera, 2026-09-19) had `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ`. I reverted `SCOPES` to that set. Caveat: Intervals' error body doesn't name the parameter, and I can't call Intervals from here, so I inferred the scope from the timing. If it still fails after this, check the CALENDAR scope names/approval for the client registration. Calendar sync will then need that scope sorted out separately.\n3. **\"Expired, reconnect\" after an hour.** Intervals' token response has no `expires_in` and no `refresh_token` (the token is long-lived until revoked). The code invented a 3600s default TTL, and with no refresh token the refresher then marked the connection expired. Fix: with no `expires_in`, `expires_at` is `None` and the refresher skips it; refresh responses missing `expires_in` are also handled.\n\nNot tested against the real Intervals.icu.\nE\npython3 -m py_compile server.py && git status --short"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6591,"cache_read_input_tokens":22365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6591},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5be2e667-3c7b-4477-9e1f-2364c34791dc","uuid":"f703d9ca-5ed9-4c27-937b-4bf3d5faa67a","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:21:55.405Z","request_id":"req_011CgS2HY5Y8bm3ypaMCRuoq","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018gcgYxBHJ8FvsGK57byssw":{"command":"cd /tmp/h-L1Pw6L && python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('''DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\n''','')\ns=s.replace('''    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh